  "question": {
    "text": "In a reaction, the time required to complete half of the reaction was found to increase 16 times when the initial concentration of the reactant was reduced to 1/4th. What is the order of the reaction?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />So n = 3<br />i.e., third order reaction.<br />&nbsp;"
  }
}